    "result_text": "All tests pass and the build succeeds.\n\n## Summary\n\nImplemented the rule rejecting owner creation when the target city already has 50+ owners, responding **409 Conflict**. Following the project's OfficeFloor function-injection conventions (mirroring the existing `EnsureUniqueHousehold` \u2192 `DuplicateHousehold` 409 flow):\n\n1. **`EnsureCityCapacity`** (`rest/function/owner/`) \u2014 a step function that reads the request DTO (`@Val OwnerFieldsDto`), counts existing owners whose city matches exactly (same comparison as `AssignCustomerCode`), and throws when the count is \u2265 50.\n\n2. **`CityAtCapacityException`** (`rest/escalation/`) \u2014 a checked exception (`extends Exception`) so it surfaces in the `throws` clause.\n\n3. **`CityAtCapacityExceptionHandler`** \u2014 responds 409 Conflict with a `ProblemDetail`, matching the existing handler pattern.\n\n4. **Escalation YAML** \u2014 `officefloor/escalation/\u2026CityAtCapacityException.yml` wiring the exception to its handler.\n\n5. **Pipeline wiring** \u2014 inserted an `ensureCityCapacity` step in `owners.POST.yml` between `ensureUniqueHousehold` and `build` (so the capacity check runs before the owner is built/saved), under `govern: [ transaction ]` like its neighbours.\n\nThe pre-existing acceptance test `coreRejectsWhenCityAtCapacity` (fills a fresh city to 50, expects the 51st to be rejected with `isConflict`) passes, and the full suite is green.",
